{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"P4cab86c1"},"owner_reference":"#3275","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"P4cab86c1\",\"feature\":\"provider-neutral-cache-bypass\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Rename backlog_list's GitHub-specific `from_github` parameter to the provider-neutral `refresh`, and add an equivalent `refresh` cache-bypass parameter to backlog_view (MCP) and CLI `view`, threading it through a restructured operations.view_item() that resolves live content via the existing authoritative head-pointer/audit-comment chain.\",\"context\":\"# Plan Context\\n\\nBacklog item: #3275. Architecture spec: `plan/architect-provider-neutral-cache-bypass.md` (read via `artifact_read(item_id=3275, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`). Feature context: `plan/feature-context-provider-neutral-cache-bypass.md`.\\n\\nThe architect spec is DECISIVE \\u2014 it contains 5 ADRs. Do not re-litigate its decisions. Implement them.\\n\\n## Repository facts verified during decomposition (do not re-derive)\\n\\n- Worktree root: `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/glittery-shimmying-summit`. Run all commands from there.\\n- All spec line references were confirmed accurate against the working tree at decomposition time: `server.py:1936/2104/2143`, `operations.py:1767/1779/1782/1806`, `operations.py:2854` (`view_item`), `sam_schema/backlog.py:95`, `sam_schema/backlog.py:110-124` (CLI `view`).\\n- `operations.list_items(from_github=...)` has exactly ONE production caller: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py:95`. Confirmed by `grep -rn \\\"from_github\\\" plugins/development-harness/ | grep -v enrich_from_github`.\\n- **`plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/` is NOT in `pyproject.toml` `testpaths` (lines 99-112).** A bare `uv run pytest` will NOT collect `tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py`. Any task touching it MUST invoke it by explicit path.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` exists and covers only `backlog add` and `backlog sync` \\u2014 it has ZERO coverage of `backlog list` and `backlog view`. Its CLI invocation pattern is `runner.invoke(app, [\\\"backlog\\\", \\\"<cmd>\\\", ...], env=_CLI_ENV)`.\\n- `tests/test_live_validation.py:286` (`test_l9_pull_refresh_from_github`) exercises the `pull` refresh path and does NOT use the `from_github=` keyword. It is a naming false positive \\u2014 leave it alone.\\n\\n## Sequencing rationale\\n\\nT1 and T3 both edit `backlog_core/operations.py`, `backlog_core/server.py`, and `sam_schema/backlog.py`. T3 depends on T1 so the rename lands first and the two never edit the same files concurrently. T2 (test renames) runs in parallel with T3 \\u2014 disjoint file sets. T4/T5/T6 fan out after T3.\\n\\n## Global constraints (apply to every task)\\n\\n- Never rename the module-level function `refresh_local_cache_from_github`, the backend method `view_enrich_from_github`, or `_overwrite_body_from_github`. Only the *parameter/kwarg* named `from_github` is in scope.\\n- ADR-2: no deprecation alias for the old `from_github` kwarg. Rename outright.\\n- ADR-4: `backlog_list_followups` / CLI `list-followups` are OUT OF SCOPE. Do not add `refresh` to them.\\n- ADR-5: no new reconciliation code. Reuse `view_enrich_from_github()` / `work_item_version()` exactly as they exist.\\n- Do not hand-edit generated docs (`docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json`, `graphify-out/graph.json`).\\n- Python invocation is always `uv run ...` \\u2014 never a bare or hardcoded interpreter.\\n\\n## Architectural context: Why this change matters\\n\\nThe backlog system maintains its own cache separate from the authoritative backend (GitHub, Beads, etc.). For GitHub specifically, the cached record uses an append-only audit-comment chain with a head pointer (backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md:780-789), NOT the visible issue body \\u2014 the body is deliberately never overwritten by reconciliation. This means asking the backend \\\"what do you have?\\\" requires calling through the exact same `view_enrich_from_github()` \\u2192 `work_item_version()` path that the reconciliation system uses, not just reading the most obvious field.\\n\\nThis item fixes two gaps:\\n1. `backlog_list` uses backend-specific parameter name `from_github` instead of provider-neutral `refresh`.\\n2. `backlog_view` has NO cache-bypass option at all \\u2014 you can verify a `list` result against live backend, but you cannot verify a `view` result, making the tool unsuitable for the validation workflow that motivated this item.\\n\\nThe fix adds `refresh` to both surfaces and gates it through the same authoritative resolution chain already proven by reconciliation, reusing zero new code paths.\\n\\n## T3 architecture: The _live_lookup_id() helper and why it's load-bearing\\n\\n**Problem:** T3 restructures `view_item()` to allow `refresh=True` on title-substring selectors (currently impossible). A naive implementation that passes the selector string directly into `view_enrich_from_github()` would crash: GitHub's backend expects a numeric issue number (`int(issue_num)` at gh_client.py:1742), and passing a title substring raises an uncaught `ValueError`.\\n\\n**Solution:** `_live_lookup_id()` resolves the cache's own knowledge of the item's backend identifier (its `number` or `issue` field) before calling the backend. This is the only safe way to do a live check for a title-matched item.\\n\\n**Identifier resolution precedence** (from spec 4.4):\\n1. `issue_num` already parsed from selector (numeric/#N/URL case) \\u2192 use it unchanged.\\n2. `item` exists locally \\u2192 return its `number` (if set), else `issue.lstrip(\\\"#\\\")` (if set), else `None`.\\n3. No local match but `item` is None \\u2192 return raw `selector.strip()` (string-id backends like Beads with a bare nanoid that hasn't synced yet).\\n4. Nothing resolvable \\u2192 return `None` (caller must skip the live check).\\n\\n**Critical:** `_live_lookup_id()` must NEVER return an empty string. `None` is the meaningful \\\"no id resolvable\\\" state; an empty string would be silently passed to `view_enrich_from_github()` and produce mysterious failures downstream.\\n\\n## T3 architecture: The view_item() truth table and why each row is load-bearing\\n\\nSpec section 4.4 contains an A-H truth table that encodes EVERY existing branch outcome of `view_item()`. The task is to restructure the branching while preserving rows C-G bit-for-bit for the `refresh=False` case (the new default), and making rows A-B opt-in rather than unconditional:\\n\\n- **Rows A-B (cached item):** Previously always did a live check unconditionally for numeric selectors. Now: live check only if `refresh=True`. DELIBERATE BEHAVIOR CHANGE (the plan's main feature).\\n- **Row H (cached item + title selector):** Previously IMPOSSIBLE \\u2014 no live check path existed. Now: live check only if `refresh=True`, via the cached item's id. NEW CAPABILITY.\\n- **Rows C-G (no cached item):** Previously fired identity-resolution live lookup unconditionally. Must stay unconditional, else \\\"item not yet synced\\\" becomes a false `ItemNotFoundError` (ADR-3 exists to prevent this exact bug). REGRESSION GUARD.\\n\\nEvery implementing agent (T3, T4) must trace through this table and verify their code satisfies every row. T4's two regression-guard tests lock rows A and C into place so future changes cannot silently revert the carefully-preserved branching.\\n\\n## T3 architecture: Backend signature harmony\\n\\nAll four backends (github_backend.py, beads_backend.py, memory_backend.py, sqlite_backend.py) expose the same `view_enrich_from_github(result: ViewItemResult, issue_num: str, repo: ...) -> bool` signature. They're all named `view_enrich_from_github` even though Beads/Memory/SQLite exist \\u2014 this is a naming artifact (GitHub was first); the function contract is backend-agnostic. Each backend implements the same interface for identity resolution and enrich. Do not rename any of them (ADR-5).\\n\\n## Testing strategy: CoVe checks and mutation guards\\n\\nT4 (operations-level tests) includes two REGRESSION GUARDS that must fail under mutation:\\n1. **Guard A:** Unconditional live call for cached numeric selectors must be gated behind `refresh`. Mutation: force `view_enrich_from_github()` to fire unconditionally \\u2192 test must fail.\\n2. **Guard C:** Identity-resolution live call for no-local-copy items must stay unconditional. Mutation: gate the call behind `refresh` \\u2192 test must fail.\\n\\nWhen you implement T3 or T4, mutation-check these guards by temporarily reverting the feature and confirming the tests go red. A test that stays green under mutation is not a test \\u2014 it's dead code.\\n\\nT5 (boundary tests) uses a similar approach: remove the forwarding kwarg from the implementation and confirm the test goes red.\\n\\n## Common implementation pitfalls and how to avoid them\\n\\n1. **Renaming function names instead of parameters:** Only `list_items`'s `from_github` kwarg is in scope (T1), NOT `refresh_local_cache_from_github()`. Grep results for `from_github` include both; the global constraints call out which are untouchable.\\n2. **Emitting empty string from `_live_lookup_id()`:** Returning `\\\"\\\"` instead of `None` when no id is resolvable is silent and downstream-deadly. Always distinguish \\\"no id\\\" (`None`) from \\\"some id\\\" (`str`).\\n3. **Passing a title string to `view_enrich_from_github()`:** This is why `_live_lookup_id()` exists. Never pass `selector` directly; always resolve to a backend-understandable identifier first.\\n4. **Losing `result.groomed = item.metadata.groomed`:** The old code set this unconditionally whenever `item` existed. The restructured code MUST preserve this on both the `refresh=True` and `refresh=False` paths inside the `if item:` block (spec 4.4).\\n5. **Gating the identity-resolution live call behind `refresh`:** This is the ADR-3 regression you're guarding against. A not-yet-synced item (no local match, but identifier resolvable via string-id backend) must still get a live lookup on `refresh=False`, else `ItemNotFoundError` is raised falsely. The `elif` in the restructured flow is carefully ordered to allow identity resolution unconditionally.\\n6. **Missing the CLI file's `env=_CLI_ENV`:** test_backlog_cli.py tests must use this environment variable; omitting it silently changes backend resolution and makes the test pass when it should fail.\\n\\n## Spec sections you MUST read in full (all other details are summarized here)\\n\\n- Spec 4.3 and 4.4 (MCP `backlog_view` and `view_item()` restructuring) \\u2014 implementation is verbatim from these sections, not a prose interpretation.\\n- Spec ADR-3 and ADR-5 \\u2014 these are the correctness constraints that make the truth table work.\\n- Spec 8 \\\"Testing Architecture\\\" \\u2014 the five specific test scenarios and why regression guards matter.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3275\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Rename backlog_list's `from_github` parameter to provider-neutral `refresh`\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T21:46:53.555323+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-28T22:41:50.729498+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T23:02:22.376661+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"## CoVe Checks\\n\\nKey claims to verify before finalizing:\\n- Claim A: `operations.list_items(from_github=...)` has exactly one production (non-test) caller.\\n- Claim B: renaming the parameter does not break any positional caller.\\n- Claim C: no MCP client contract outside this repo depends on the `from_github` key.\\n\\nVerification questions:\\n1. Does `grep -rn 'list_items(' plugins/ scripts/ --include=*.py` reveal any caller besides `sam_schema/backlog.py:95` and `backlog_core/server.py:2143` that passes this parameter?\\n2. Does any caller pass `list_items` arguments positionally rather than by keyword?\\n3. Does the renamed Field description still mention GitHub, Beads, or any other backend by name?\\n4. Did the `if refresh:` guard preserve the exact same body (`refresh_local_cache_from_github(repo, label, output=out)`) with no changes?\\n\\nEvidence to collect: the grep output for question 1; the signature-inspection output; the `git diff` for `operations.py` lines around 1806.\\n\\nRevision rule: if question 1 reveals an unlisted caller, update it in this same task and report it in the handoff as a spec deviation (the architect spec asserts a single caller). If question 2 finds a positional caller, keep the parameter position fixed and note it.\",\"description\":\"The backlog MCP tools are provider-neutral (backend can be GitHub, Beads, SQLite, or Memory), but `backlog_list`'s cache-refresh parameter is named `from_github`, naming one specific backend. Its sibling reconcile tool already uses the neutral `full_refresh`, and the CLI already exposes `--refresh` \\u2014 so the CLI currently has to translate its own `refresh` variable into a `from_github=` kwarg. This task removes that mismatch by renaming the parameter end to end.\\n\\nThis is a pure rename. No behavior changes, no new capability. Architect spec sections 4.1, 4.2 and ADR-1, ADR-2 govern.\",\"objective\":\"The cache-refresh capability on `backlog_list` (MCP), `operations.list_items()`, and its sole internal caller is named `refresh` instead of `from_github`, with no backend named anywhere in the parameter or its description.\",\"requirements\":\"1. In `backlog_core/server.py`, rename the `backlog_list` tool parameter `from_github` to `refresh`, keeping `Annotated[bool, Field(description=...)] = False`. Rewrite the description to name no specific backend \\u2014 use: `\\\"Refresh the local cache from the configured backend before listing\\\"`.\\n2. Update the `backlog_list` docstring line at server.py:2104 to `Use refresh=true to refresh the local cache from the backend before listing.`\\n3. Update the forwarding call at server.py:2143 to `refresh=refresh,`.\\n4. In `backlog_core/operations.py`, rename `list_items`'s `from_github: bool = False` parameter to `refresh: bool = False`, keeping it in the SAME positional slot so no caller's positional arguments shift.\\n5. Update `list_items`'s docstring summary and `Args:` entry to describe `refresh` in provider-neutral terms (say \\\"the configured backend\\\", not \\\"GitHub Issues\\\").\\n6. Update the guard at operations.py:1806 to `if refresh:`.\\n7. In `sam_schema/backlog.py:95`, change `from_github=refresh,` to `refresh=refresh,`.\",\"constraints\":\"- Do NOT rename the module-level function `refresh_local_cache_from_github` \\u2014 it is a different identifier and is out of scope.\\n- Do NOT add a deprecation alias, a `**kwargs` shim, or a `DeprecationWarning` forwarder. ADR-2 decided an outright rename because the sole production caller is updated in this same change.\\n- Do NOT change the CLI `--refresh` flag name or the CLI's local `refresh` variable.\\n- Do NOT touch `backlog_list_followups` or CLI `list-followups` (ADR-4, out of scope).\\n- Do NOT edit any test file in this task \\u2014 test updates are T2's scope. Leave the suite red on the renamed call sites; T2 fixes it.\\n- Do NOT edit `skills/backlog/SKILL.md` or `skills/backlog/README.md` \\u2014 that is T6's scope.\\n- Do NOT change the parameter's position in either signature.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (modified)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` (modified)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` (modified)\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `grep -rn 'from_github' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py | grep -v 'refresh_local_cache_from_github' | grep -v 'enrich_from_github' | grep -v '_overwrite_body_from_github'` produces zero output lines.\\n2. `uv run python -c \\\"import inspect,sys; sys.path.insert(0,'plugins/development-harness'); from backlog_core import operations; p=inspect.signature(operations.list_items).parameters; assert 'refresh' in p and p['refresh'].default is False; assert 'from_github' not in p; print('OK')\\\"` prints `OK`.\\n3. The `backlog_list` MCP tool's `refresh` Field description contains no occurrence of the string `GitHub` (case-insensitive) \\u2014 the parameter is provider-neutral in wording, not just in name.\\n4. `list_items`'s `refresh` parameter occupies the same positional index that `from_github` occupied, so no positional caller breaks.\\n5. `uv run ruff check` and `uv run ty check` both pass on all three modified files with no new diagnostics.\\n6. No deprecation alias, shim, or backward-compatibility forwarder for `from_github` exists anywhere in the diff.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/glittery-shimmying-summit && grep -rn 'from_github' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py | grep -v 'refresh_local_cache_from_github' | grep -v 'enrich_from_github' | grep -v '_overwrite_body_from_github'` and confirm zero output.\\n2. Run the signature assertion in acceptance criterion 2 and confirm it prints `OK`.\\n3. Run `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` and `uv run ty check` on the same three files; confirm both clean.\\n4. Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` and record which tests now fail. Expect failures ONLY on the `from_github=` keyword call sites T2 will fix. If any test fails for a reason OTHER than the renamed keyword, stop and report \\u2014 that indicates the rename changed behavior, which it must not.\\n5. Run `git add plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` then `git commit -m \\\"refactor(backlog_core): rename backlog_list from_github parameter to refresh\\\"`.\",\"context_notes\":\"Architect spec: `artifact_read(item_id=3275, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`, sections 4.1, 4.2, ADR-1, ADR-2.\\n\\nExact sites (all line numbers verified at decomposition time; re-confirm before editing since your own edits shift them):\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1936` \\u2014 the `Annotated[bool, Field(...)]` parameter declaration.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2104` \\u2014 docstring line `Use from_github=true to refresh the local cache from GitHub before listing.`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2143` \\u2014 forwarding kwarg `from_github=from_github,` inside the `operations.list_items(...)` call.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1767` \\u2014 `from_github: bool = False,` in the `list_items` signature.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1779` \\u2014 docstring summary line.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1782` \\u2014 the `Args:` entry for the parameter.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1806` \\u2014 `if from_github:` guard.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py:95` \\u2014 `from_github=refresh,` becomes `refresh=refresh,`.\\n\\nThe CLI's local variable at `sam_schema/backlog.py:79-81` is ALREADY named `refresh` and its flag is ALREADY `--refresh`. Do not change the CLI flag.\",\"handoff\":\"Return:\\n- The exact `git diff --stat` for the three modified files.\\n- The list of tests that failed after the rename, with confirmation that every failure is attributable to the renamed keyword and nothing else. T2 consumes this list.\\n- Confirmation of the sole-caller claim (CoVe question 1 output), or the additional callers found.\\n- Any blocked item and what is needed.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T2\",\"title\":\"Update rename-affected tests from `from_github` to `refresh`\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-pytest-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T21:46:53.556813+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-28T23:15:06.808489+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T23:22:24.467628+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"## CoVe Checks\\n\\nKey claims to verify:\\n- Claim A: `tests/test_live_validation.py:286` is a naming false positive and needs no change.\\n- Claim B: every remaining `from_github` string in the test tree refers to a function name, not the renamed parameter.\\n- Claim C: no test was dropped by a function-name collision after renaming.\\n\\nVerification questions:\\n1. Read `tests/test_live_validation.py` around line 286 \\u2014 does the test body pass `from_github=` to anything, or does it only exercise the `pull` path?\\n2. For each surviving `from_github` grep hit, is the matched text part of a longer identifier (`refresh_local_cache_from_github`, `view_enrich_from_github`, `fetch_tasks_from_github`, `_overwrite_body_from_github`) or a bare parameter?\\n3. After renaming `test_list_items_from_github_calls_refresh` and `test_list_from_github`, does a function with the new name already exist in the same module (which would silently shadow one of them)?\\n4. Is the pytest collected count for every modified file unchanged from HEAD?\\n\\nEvidence to collect: the read of `test_live_validation.py` around line 286; the annotated grep output; the before/after `--collect-only` counts.\\n\\nRevision rule: if question 3 reveals a name collision, choose a distinct non-colliding name and report the choice. If question 1 shows `test_live_validation.py` DOES use the keyword, update it and note the spec deviation.\",\"description\":\"T1 renamed `list_items`'s `from_github` kwarg and `backlog_list`'s MCP parameter to `refresh`, which breaks every existing test that passes the old name. This task updates those call sites and the two test function names that embed the old parameter name.\\n\\nThis is a mechanical update, not a coverage change. Do not add new test scenarios here \\u2014 new coverage is T4 and T5's scope.\",\"objective\":\"Every existing test that passes `from_github` as a keyword argument or as an MCP payload dict key is updated to `refresh`, and the full backlog test suite passes again after T1's rename.\",\"requirements\":\"1. In `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`, change every `list_items(from_github=...)` keyword to `list_items(refresh=...)` at all ten call sites.\\n2. Rename `test_list_items_from_github_calls_refresh` to `test_list_items_refresh_calls_refresh_local_cache` and rewrite its docstring so it describes `refresh` rather than `from_github`, preserving the existing Tests/How/Why docstring structure used in that file.\\n3. In `tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py`, change `list_items(from_github=True, label=\\\"review\\\")` to `list_items(refresh=True, label=\\\"review\\\")`.\\n4. In `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`, change the MCP payload dict key `\\\"from_github\\\"` to `\\\"refresh\\\"` and update the two `call_kwargs[\\\"from_github\\\"]` assertions to `call_kwargs[\\\"refresh\\\"]`, plus the docstring at line 203