ugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` passes with zero failures (explicit path required \\u2014 this directory is not in `testpaths`).\\n3. `grep -rn 'from_github' plugins/development-harness/tests/ plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/ | grep -v 'refresh_local_cache_from_github' | grep -v 'enrich_from_github' | grep -v 'fetch_tasks_from_github' | grep -v 'test_l9_pull_refresh_from_github' | grep -v 'title_from_github_creation' | grep -v 'item_ref_from_github' | grep -v 'not_imported_from_github'` produces zero output lines.\\n4. The test collected count for each modified file is identical before and after the change \\u2014 no test was accidentally dropped or duplicated by a rename collision.\\n5. No assertion in the diff was weakened, removed, or made conditional.\\n6. `uv run ruff check` passes on all four modified test files.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/glittery-shimmying-summit && uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` and confirm zero failures.\\n2. Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` (explicit path) and confirm zero failures.\\n3. Run the acceptance-criterion-3 grep and confirm zero output.\\n4. Run `uv run pytest <each modified file> --collect-only -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov | tail -1` and compare the collected count against `git stash`-free baseline captured from `git show HEAD:<path>`; confirm counts are unchanged.\\n5. Run `git add plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` then `git commit -m \\\"test(backlog_core): update from_github call sites to refresh\\\"`.\",\"context_notes\":\"Architect spec section 8, \\\"Rename-affected (update, do not just re-run)\\\".\\n\\nExact sites (verified at decomposition time; line numbers shift as you edit, so match on content):\\n\\n**`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`** \\u2014 `list_items(from_github=...)` at lines 450, 712, 735, 758, 780, 797, 844, 868, 894, 1760. Also rename the test function `test_list_items_from_github_calls_refresh` (line 784) to `test_list_items_refresh_calls_refresh_local_cache`, and update its docstring (lines 785-789) which references `from_github` three times.\\n\\n**`plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py:111`** \\u2014 `list_items(from_github=True, label=\\\"review\\\")`.\\n\\n**`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py`** \\u2014 MCP payload dict key and assertions at lines 197, 203 (docstring), 206, 209.\\n\\n**`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py`** \\u2014 line 115 (comment), 116 (test function name `test_list_from_github`), 119 (`{\\\"from_github\\\": True}`), 1516 (comment), 1517 (`{\\\"from_github\\\": True, \\\"include_closed\\\": True}`).\\n\\n**`plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py:286`** \\u2014 `test_l9_pull_refresh_from_github`. Verified at decomposition time: this exercises the `pull` refresh path and does NOT use the `from_github=` keyword. It is a naming false positive. Confirm this yourself, then LEAVE IT UNCHANGED.\\n\\n**Critical runner note:** `plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog/` is NOT listed in `pyproject.toml` `testpaths` (lines 99-112). A bare `uv run pytest` will not collect `test_reconciliation_wrapper.py`. You MUST invoke it by explicit path to verify your change to it.\",\"handoff\":\"Return:\\n- Pass/fail summary for both pytest invocations, including the explicit-path run of `tests_backlog/`.\\n- Explicit confirmation of the `test_live_validation.py:286` finding (false positive, or updated).\\n- Before/after collected counts per modified file.\\n- Any test that failed for a reason other than the renamed keyword, with the traceback.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T3\",\"title\":\"Add provider-neutral `refresh` cache-bypass to view_item, MCP backlog_view, and CLI view\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-cli-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"high\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T21:46:53.556969+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-28T23:10:35.112261+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T23:45:20.529686+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"## CoVe Checks\\n\\nThis task carries the plan's highest accuracy risk. Run these checks before committing.\\n\\nKey claims to verify:\\n- Claim A: passing a raw title string into `view_enrich_from_github()` reaches `int(issue_num)` in `gh_client.py` and raises an uncaught `ValueError`.\\n- Claim B: no existing test asserts the previously-unconditional live call for an ALREADY-CACHED numeric-selector item (ADR-3's no-regression basis).\\n- Claim C: all four backends share the identical `view_enrich_from_github(result, issue_num: str, repo) -> bool` signature, so `_live_lookup_id()`'s `str` return type is correct for every backend.\\n- Claim D: the restructured flow preserves truth-table cases C through G bit-for-bit.\\n\\nVerification questions:\\n1. Read `gh_client.py` around line 1742 \\u2014 is `int(issue_num)` actually reached on the title-string path, and is there truly no enclosing `except BacklogException` or `except ValueError`?\\n2. Run `grep -rn 'view_enrich_from_github' plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests plugins/development-harness/tests_backlog` \\u2014 does any existing test assert that this is called for a cached numeric item? If one does, ADR-3's no-regression basis is wrong and you must report it rather than deleting the test.\\n3. Run `grep -rn 'def view_enrich_from_github' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/` \\u2014 do all four implementations share the same signature?\\n4. For each truth-table row C, D, E, F, G: which exact line of your new code executes, and does it produce the same outcome the old code produced?\\n5. When `item` exists, is `result.groomed = item.metadata.groomed` still executed on BOTH the `refresh=True` and `refresh=False` paths? (The old code set it unconditionally inside `if item:` \\u2014 losing it on the default path would be a silent regression.)\\n6. Does the `refresh=True` + enrich-failure path APPEND a warning rather than raising, for a cached item?\\n\\nEvidence to collect: the `gh_client.py` read; both grep outputs; the annotated per-row trace; the `git diff` of the branch block.\\n\\nRevision rule: if question 2 finds a contradicting test, STOP \\u2014 do not modify or delete it. Report it as an ADR-3 contradiction and request guidance. If question 5 shows `result.groomed` is not set on both paths, fix it before committing.\",\"description\":\"`backlog_view` has no cache-bypass option at all. It cannot answer \\\"did this content actually reach the backend?\\\" \\u2014 the real problem that motivated item #3275. Meanwhile its numeric-selector path fires an UNCONDITIONAL live call on every view-by-number, even when a local cached copy already exists, and its title-substring path can never do a live check at all.\\n\\nThis task restructures `view_item()`'s branching so that a live check is an explicit opt-in for already-cached items (any selector shape), while identity-resolution live calls \\u2014 the ones that answer \\\"does this item exist anywhere?\\\" \\u2014 stay unconditional so a not-yet-synced item never regresses into a false `ItemNotFoundError`.\\n\\nThis is the highest-risk task in the plan. The architect spec section 4.4 contains an A-H truth table that encodes every existing branch outcome. Preserving it exactly for `refresh=False` (except cases A and B, which become opt-in by design) is the correctness bar.\",\"objective\":\"`operations.view_item()` accepts `refresh: bool = False` and, when True, forces a live-backend check through the existing authoritative resolution chain for every selector shape including title substrings; MCP `backlog_view` and CLI `view` both expose and forward it.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Add the private helper `_live_lookup_id(item: BacklogItem | None, issue_num: str | None, selector: str) -> str | None` to `backlog_core/operations.py`, placed immediately above `view_item()`. Implement exactly the contract in spec section 4.4:\\n   - `issue_num` truthy \\u2192 return it unchanged.\\n   - else if `item is not None` \\u2192 return `str(item.number)` if `item.number` is set; else `item.issue.lstrip(\\\"#\\\") or None` if `item.issue` is set; else `None`.\\n   - else \\u2192 return `selector.strip() or None`.\\n   Use the docstring given verbatim in spec section 4.4.\\n2. Add `refresh: bool = False` to `view_item()`'s signature, positioned immediately after `section`, and document it in the existing Google-style `Args:` block.\\n3. Replace `view_item()`'s existing branch block with the restructured control flow given verbatim in spec section 4.4.\\n4. Add a `refresh` parameter to the MCP `backlog_view` tool in `server.py`, positioned immediately after `selector`, using the `Annotated[bool, Field(description=...)] = False` text given verbatim in spec section 4.3.\\n5. Forward `refresh=refresh` into the `asyncio.to_thread(operations.view_item, ...)` call in `backlog_view`.\\n6. Add `refresh: Annotated[bool, typer.Option(\\\"--refresh\\\", help=\\\"Bypass the local cache and validate against the live backend\\\")] = False` to the CLI `view` command in `sam_schema/backlog.py`, and forward `refresh=refresh` into its `operations.view_item(...)` call.\",\"constraints\":\"- Do NOT write any new reconciliation, head-pointer, or audit-comment resolution logic (ADR-5). Call `view_enrich_from_github()` exactly as the existing code does.\\n- Do NOT modify `view_enrich_from_github()` in any of the four backend files, `gh_client.py`, `backend_types.py`'s `SyncProvider` protocol, or `reconcile()`.\\n- Do NOT ever pass a raw title-substring selector into `view_enrich_from_github()`. That is what `_live_lookup_id()` exists to prevent.\\n- Do NOT gate the identity-resolution live call (no local copy) behind `refresh`. Cases C through G in the truth table must fire unconditionally, or a not-yet-synced item raises a false `ItemNotFoundError` (ADR-3).\\n- Do NOT add a new field to `ViewItemResult` or `ViewItemResultCompact` (spec section 5). Reuse the existing `warnings: list[str]` for the \\\"backend unreachable\\\" message; use the exact existing message string `\\\"backend unreachable \\u2014 sections_index reflects provider-backed record, may be stale\\\"`.\\n- Do NOT introduce an enum, `Literal`, or `StrEnum` for the flag \\u2014 plain `bool` (spec section 6).\\n- Do NOT let `_live_lookup_id()` return an empty string. `None` is the meaningful \\\"no id resolvable\\\" state and callers must skip the live call on it.\\n- Do NOT add `refresh` to `backlog_list_followups` or CLI `list-followups` (ADR-4).\\n- Do NOT edit test files. T4 and T5 own test coverage.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` (modified \\u2014 new `_live_lookup_id` helper, `view_item` signature and branch restructure)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (modified \\u2014 `backlog_view` `refresh` parameter and forwarding)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` (modified \\u2014 CLI `view --refresh` flag and forwarding)\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `uv run python -c \\\"import inspect,sys; sys.path.insert(0,'plugins/development-harness'); from backlog_core import operations; p=inspect.signature(operations.view_item).parameters; ks=list(p); assert 'refresh' in p and p['refresh'].default is False; assert ks[ks.index('section')+1]=='refresh'; print('OK')\\\"` prints `OK`.\\n2. `uv run python -m sam_schema.cli backlog view --help` output contains `--refresh`.\\n3. Every row of the architect spec section 4.4 A-H truth table is satisfied by the implemented control flow, demonstrated by a written row-by-row trace in the handoff. Specifically: case C (numeric selector, no cached item, `refresh=False`) still performs a live lookup and does not raise; case G (non-numeric selector, no cached item, non-string-id backend) still raises `ItemNotFoundError`.\\n4. `_live_lookup_id()` returns `None` \\u2014 never an empty string and never the raw selector \\u2014 when `item` is not None but has neither `number` nor `issue` set; and the caller skips `view_enrich_from_github()` entirely on a `None` return.\\n5. A title-substring selector with `refresh=True` calls `view_enrich_from_github()` with the cached item's `number`/`issue`-derived identifier, never the title text.\\n6. `ViewItemResult` and `ViewItemResultCompact` in `models.py` are byte-identical to HEAD \\u2014 `git diff HEAD -- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` is empty.\\n7. `git diff HEAD --stat` touches exactly the three files in Expected Outputs and no backend file, `gh_client.py`, or `backend_types.py`.\\n8. `uv run ruff check` and `uv run ty check` pass clean on all three modified files.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run the signature assertion from acceptance criterion 1 and confirm it prints `OK`.\\n2. Run `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/glittery-shimmying-summit && uv run python -m sam_schema.cli backlog view --help 2>&1 | grep -- '--refresh'` and confirm the flag appears with its help text.\\n3. Run `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` and `uv run ty check` on the same three files; confirm both clean.\\n4. Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` and confirm zero failures \\u2014 no pre-existing view test may regress.\\n5. Run `git diff HEAD --stat` and confirm only the three Expected Outputs files appear.\\n6. Write the row-by-row A-H truth table trace into the handoff, citing the specific implemented line for each row.\\n7. Run `git add plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` then `git commit -m \\\"feat(backlog_core): add refresh cache-bypass to backlog_view and CLI view\\\"`.\",\"context_notes\":\"Architect spec: `artifact_read(item_id=3275, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`. Read sections 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 5, 6, and ADR-3 and ADR-5 IN FULL before writing any code. Section 4.4 contains the exact restructured control-flow snippet, the `_live_lookup_id()` docstring and contract, and the A-H truth table. Implement that snippet \\u2014 do not invent an alternative structure.\\n\\nCurrent code:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:2854` \\u2014 `view_item()` signature.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \\u2014 the branch block starting `item = find_item(...)` / `issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)` / `result: ViewItemResult = ...` / `if issue_num:` ... `elif not item:` ... This block is what section 4.4 replaces.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:2392` \\u2014 the `backlog_view` MCP tool; `selector` is its first parameter.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` ~2591 \\u2014 the `await asyncio.to_thread(operations.view_item, selector=..., include_content=..., offset=..., limit=..., show=parsed_show, since=..., section=..., output=out)` call.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py:110-124` \\u2014 CLI `view` command and its `operations.view_item(...)` call.\\n\\n**Why `_live_lookup_id()` must exist:** passing a raw title-substring selector into `view_enrich_from_github()` reaches `int(issue_num)` in `gh_client.py:1742`, which raises an uncaught `ValueError` \\u2014 no `except BacklogException` catches it there. A naive `refresh` implementation that forwards `selector` for title matches would crash. The helper resolves the cached item's own `number`/`issue` instead.\\n\\nAll four backends (github, beads, memory, sqlite) share the identical `view_enrich_from_github(result, issue_num: str, repo) -> bool` signature \\u2014 do not change any of them (ADR-5).\\n## ADR-3 Contradiction Found \\u2014 Blocking\\n\\nImplementation of `_live_lookup_id()` and the restructured `view_item()` branching (spec \\u00a74.4, ADR-3) is complete and matches the spec verbatim, with one adaptation: `BacklogItem` has no `.number` field (only `.issue: str`), so `_live_lookup_id()` uses `getattr(item, \\\"number\\\", None)` defensively \\u2014 it always falls through to `item.issue.lstrip(\\\"#\\\")` today. Flagging this as a minor spec/code mismatch, not blocking on its own.\\n\\nThe blocking issue is CoVe question 2. ADR-3's premise is: \\\"no test in `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` asserts the previously-unconditional numeric-selector live call for an already-cached item, so no test regression.\\\" That check only grepped one file. A full run of `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests` against my restructured code (with T1+T2's rename already merged in) produces **52 new failures**, all in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/` (test_section_filter_error_dict.py:13, test_view_sections_metadata_sync.py:12, test_view_pagination_section_index.py:9, test_view_over_budget_gate.py:7, test_view_section_filter.py:3, test_view_live_sections.py:3, test_section_filter_miss.py:2, test_concurrent_writes.py:2, test_section_boundary_scanner_live_3152.py:1). Verified against baseline (git worktree at T1's commit, before my changes): 0 of these 52 fail on baseline; the pre-existing 17 baseline failures are unrelated (list_items from_github rename, already fixed by T2's commit, plus one unrelated PLR lint-gate test).\\n\\nRoot cause: all 52 tests use the shared `backlog_core/tests/_view_test_helpers.py::_configure_memory_view` fixture, which patches a numeric-selector item's backend `view_enrich_from_github` to inject a live body/sections, then assert on the resulting `result.body`/`result.sections`/`result.sections_index`. This is exactly Case A (cached item + numeric selector) \\u2014 which this spec deliberately gates behind `refresh=False` by default. These tests never call `view_item(..., refresh=True)`, so under the new default they get an empty/stale body and fail.\\n\\nMost telling example: `test_concurrent_writes.py::test_second_groom_write_does_not_clobber_first_sections_on_view` asserts \\\"the fix must prefer live data\\\" over a stale local cache \\u2014 its entire premise is that Case A's live check must be unconditional. This is a prior regression-guard test whose design assumption directly contradicts ADR-3.\\n\\nPer this task's revision rule: STOPPING here. Have NOT modified or deleted any test file (T4/T5 own tests; I only ran them read-only). Code changes to the three Expected Outputs files are complete and clean (ruff, ty, signature/CLI acceptance criteria all pass) but NOT committed as done, pending a decision on ADR-3.\\n\\nOptions for guidance:\\n1. Revise ADR-3: keep Case A's live call unconditional (today's behavior) and only add `refresh` as new opt-in capability for Case H (title selectors) \\u2014 i.e. `refresh` only ever adds live checks, never removes an existing one. This would make my restructure additive-only and these 52 tests would need no changes.\\n2. Keep ADR-3 as specified and treat these 52 tests as needing rewrite to pass `refresh=True` explicitly \\u2014 but that is a large, cross-cutting test-file change well beyond T4/T5's currently scoped new-test additions, and re-opens the file-ownership boundary between T3/T4/T5.\\n\\nRequesting guidance on which direction to take before proceeding.\\n## Handoff: Corrected A-H Truth Table and CoVe Answers\\n\\nADR-3 corrected per team-lead decision: `refresh` is additive-only. Case A/B (cached item + numeric/#N/URL selector) stay unconditional, exactly matching pre-existing behavior. Only Case H (cached item + title selector, `issue_num` is falsy) is new/opt-in. Fix applied: the `if item:` branch's live-check guard changed from `if refresh:` to `if issue_num or refresh:` (operations.py, `view_item()`).\\n\\n## Corrected row-by-row trace (operations.py `view_item()`, current code)\\n\\n- **Row A** (issue_num truthy, item cached): `if item:` \\u2192 `if issue_num or refresh:` \\u2192 `issue_num` truthy so always True \\u2192 live-checks unconditionally via `_live_lookup_id()` (returns `issue_num` unchanged, first branch of the helper). Matches pre-existing behavior bit-for-bit.\\n- **Row B** (issue_num truthy, item cached, enrich fails): same branch; `enriched=False` \\u2192 `out.warnings.append(\\\"backend unreachable \\u2014 sections_index reflects provider-backed record, may be stale\\\")`, no exception (item exists). Matches pre-existing behavior.\\n- **Row C** (issue_num truthy, no item): `elif issue_num or get_config().backend.issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\":` \\u2192 True via `issue_num` \\u2192 live lookup via `_live_lookup_id()` (returns `issue_num`) \\u2192 no exception on success. Unchanged, unconditional (identity-resolution branch, per ADR-3's original unconditional intent \\u2014 this part was never in question).\\n- **Row D** (issue_num truthy, no item, enrich fails): same branch, `enriched=False` \\u2192 `raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)`. Unchanged.\\n- **Row E/F** (issue_num falsy, no item, string-id backend): `elif ... or get_config().backend.issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\":` \\u2192 True \\u2192 `_live_lookup_id(None, None, selector)` \\u2192 third branch, `selector.strip() or None` (bare nanoid) \\u2192 live lookup fires unconditionally. Unchanged.\\n- **Row G** (issue_num falsy, no item, non-string-id backend): both `if`/`elif` conditions False \\u2192 `else: raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)`. Unchanged.\\n- **Row H** (issue_num falsy, item cached \\u2014 title selector): `if item:` \\u2192 `if issue_num or refresh:` \\u2192 only True when caller passes `refresh=True` \\u2192 `_live_lookup_id(item, None, selector)` \\u2192 second branch: `getattr(item, \\\"number\\\", None)` (see note below) then `item.issue.lstrip(\\\"#\\\") or None` \\u2014 never the raw title. New capability, opt-in only, exactly as designed.\\n\\n## `_live_lookup_id()` as implemented\\n\\n```python\\ndef _live_lookup_id(item: BacklogItem | None, issue_num: str | None, selector: str) -> str | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Resolve the identifier to pass to view_enrich_from_github() for a live check.\\n\\n    Precedence: an already-parsed numeric selector; else the cached item's own\\n    known issue number/id (for a title-selector match \\u2014 never the raw title\\n    text, which the GitHub backend cannot resolve); else the raw selector\\n    (bare beads nanoid with no local match yet).\\n\\n    Returns:\\n        The identifier to pass to view_enrich_from_github(), or None when no\\n        identifier of any kind is resolvable. Never an empty string.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if issue_num:\\n        return issue_num\\n    if item is not None:\\n        number = getattr(item, \\\"number\\\", None)\\n        if number:\\n            return str(number)\\n        return item.issue.lstrip(\\\"#\\\") or None\\n    return selector.strip() or None\\n```\\n\\nNote (spec/code mismatch, non-blocking): `BacklogItem` (models.py:953) has no `.number` field, only `.issue: str`. Used `getattr(item, \\\"number\\\", None)` defensively so the contract is safe against the model as it actually exists; it always falls through to `item.issue` today. Never returns `\\\"\\\"` \\u2014 confirmed via `item.issue.lstrip(\\\"#\\\") or None` and `selector.strip() or None`, both of which coerce falsy/empty results to `None`.\\n\\n## CoVe answers\\n\\n1. Confirmed: `gh_client.py:1742` reaches `int(issue_num)` inside a `try/except (BacklogError, GithubException)` \\u2014 no `ValueError` catch. A raw title string reaching this line raises uncaught. `_live_lookup_id()` prevents this by never passing `selector` for a title match.\\n2. Initial grep (scoped to `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` only, per the original CoVe question) found none \\u2014 but the full suite run found 52 tests in `backlog_core/tests/` that depended on it via the shared `_view_test_helpers.py::_configure_memory_view` fixture. Reported as an ADR-3 contradiction; team-lead resolved by making `refresh` additive-only (see task's earlier \\\"ADR-3 Contradiction Found\\\" section for full detail). All 52 pass again after the fix, confirmed by a clean full-suite run (3720 passed, 0 failed).\\n3. Confirmed: all four backends (github_backend.py:546, beads_backend.py:662, sqlite_backend.py:797, memory_backend.py:438) share the identical `view_enrich_from_github(self, result: ViewItemResult, issue_num: str, repo: str = \\\"\\\") -> bool` signature.\\n5. Confirmed: `result.groomed = item.metadata.groomed` executes unconditionally inside `if item:`, outside the `if issue_num or refresh:` block \\u2014 runs on every path where `item` exists, regardless of whether a live check happened.\\n\\n## Final verification\\n\\n- `models.py` untouched: `git diff HEAD -- plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` empty.\\n- `git diff HEAD --stat` (pre-commit) touched exactly the three Expected Outputs files.\\n- Signature check, CLI `--help` check, `ruff check`, `ty check` all pass on the three modified files.\\n- Full suite (`plugins/development-harness/tests backlog_core/tests sam_schema/tests`): 3720 passed, 0 failed, 39 skipped, 5 xfailed.\\n- Committed as `6520637b6` (correction) on top of `488d5c542` (initial implementation) and `3efc4d7df` (T2's rename, landed concurrently in this shared worktree).\",\"handoff\":\"Return:\\n- The full row-by-row A-H truth-table trace, each row citing the implemented line that produces its outcome.\\n- The `_live_lookup_id()` implementation as written (this exact text is load-bearing for T4's tests).\\n- Answers to CoVe questions 1, 2, 3, and 5 with their evidence.\\n- Confirmation that `models.py` is untouched and that no backend file, `gh_client.py`, or `backend_types.py` appears in the diff.\\n- Any ADR contradiction found, with the evidence, and what guidance is needed.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"high\"},{\"id\":\"T4\",\"title\":\"Add operations-level test coverage for view_item's refresh control flow\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-pytest-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T2\",\"T3\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T21:46:53.557084+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-29T00:21:26.118255+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"## CoVe Checks\\n\\nKey claims to verify:\\n- Claim A: each of the five scenarios has no pre-existing coverage in the file.\\n- Claim B: the two regression-guard tests genuinely fail when the behavior they guard is reverted (a test that passes under both behaviors guards nothing).\\n- Claim C: the identifier assertions match `_live_lookup_id()`'s ACTUAL implemented precedence, not the spec's prose paraphrase.\\n\\nVerification questions:\\n1. Does `grep -n 'def test_view_item' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` reveal an existing test already covering any of the five scenarios?\\n2. For the scenario-2 guard: when you force an unconditional live call, does the test actually go red? Record the failure output.\\n3. For the scenario-3 guard: when you gate the identity-resolution call behind `refresh`, does the test actually go red? Record the failure output.\\n4. Does T3's handoff `_live_lookup_id()` implementation resolve `item.number` before `item.issue`, and does your scenario-1 fixture set the field you are asserting on?\\n5. Does the scenario-5 test assert the exact warning string the implementation appends, or a substring of it that would survive a benign rewording?\\n\\nEvidence to collect: the grep output for question 1; the red-then-green outputs for questions 2 and 3; the coverage report.\\n\\nRevision rule: if either regression guard does NOT go red under mutation, the test is not asserting what it claims \\u2014 rewrite it and re-run the mutation check. If question 1 finds pre-existing coverage, extend that test rather than adding a duplicate, and say so in the handoff.\",\"description\":\"T3 restructured `view_item()`'s branching: the numeric-selector live call became opt-in for already-cached items, title-selector cached items gained an opt-in live check that was previously impossible, and a new `_live_lookup_id()` helper resolves which identifier to send to the backend. None of these branches has existing coverage.\\n\\nThe two regression-guard tests matter most: one locks in the new `refresh=False` default (the deliberate behavior change), and one proves that an item with no local copy still gets a live lookup regardless of the flag \\u2014 the false-`ItemNotFoundError` bug ADR-3 exists to prevent.\",\"objective\":\"`operations.view_item()`'s five new/changed control-flow branches each have a dedicated passing test, including regression guards that lock in the new `refresh=False` default and prove a not-yet-synced item still resolves.\",\"requirements\":\"Add these tests to `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`, one test function per scenario:\\n\\n1. Cached item + title-substring selector + `refresh=True` \\u2192 `view_enrich_from_github` is called, and the identifier argument equals the item's `number`/`issue`-derived id. Assert explicitly that the argument is NOT the raw title string.\\n2. Cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` \\u2192 `view_enrich_from_github` is NOT called. This locks in the new default and is the plan's primary regression-risk case; name it so its intent is obvious.\\n3. No cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` \\u2192 the live lookup still fires and no `ItemNotFoundError` is raised. Regression guard for ADR-3.\\n4. No cached item + beads-style nanoid selector on a string-id backend + `refresh=False` \\u2192 the live lookup still fires.\\n5. Cached item + `refresh=True` + the item has neither `number` nor `issue` set \\u2192 a warning is appended to the result, no exception is raised, and `view_enrich_from_github` is NOT called.\\n\\nEach test must use the file's existing docstring convention and assert on observable behavior (call/no-call, argument values, warnings list contents, exception raised or not) rather than on internal state.\",\"constraints\":\"- Do NOT modify `backlog_core/operations.py` or any other production file. If a test cannot be written without a production change, stop and report it.\\n- Do NOT weaken, skip, or `xfail` any existing test to accommodate the new ones.\\n- Do NOT assert on `_live_lookup_id()` directly as a unit. Test it through `view_item()`'s observable behavior \\u2014 it is a private helper and its signature is not a public contract.\\n- Do NOT make any network call. Patch `backlog_core.operations.view_enrich_from_github` in every test.\\n- Do NOT duplicate an existing test's scenario. Check the file for prior coverage of each scenario before adding.\\n- Do NOT add tests for MCP `backlog_view` or the CLI here \\u2014 those are T5's scope.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` (modified \\u2014 five new test functions)\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. All five scenarios from Requirements have a dedicated, passing test function; `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` reports zero failures.\\n2. The scenario-1 test asserts on the actual identifier argument passed to `view_enrich_from_github` and includes a negative assertion that it does not equal the raw title selector string.\\n3. The scenario-2 test fails if the `refresh=False` default is ever reverted to an unconditional live call \\u2014 verify this by temporarily forcing the call and confirming the test goes red, then reverting.\\n4. The scenario-3 test fails if the identity-resolution live call is ever gated behind `refresh` \\u2014 verify the same way.\\n5. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py --cov=backlog_core.operations --cov-report=term-missing -q -p no:cacheprovider` reports at least 90% line coverage across `view_item()` and `_live_lookup_id()`.\\n6. No test in the file was modified, skipped, or removed; the collected count increased by exactly five.\\n7. `uv run ruff check` passes on the modified file.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. Run `cd /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/.claude/worktrees/glittery-shimmying-summit && uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov` and confirm zero failures.\\n2. Mutation-check the two regression guards: temporarily edit `view_item()` to (a) call `view_enrich_from_github` unconditionally for cached items, confirm the scenario-2 test fails; then (b) gate the no-local-copy live call behind `refresh`, confirm the scenario-3 test fails. Revert both edits and re-run to confirm green. Report both red/green transitions as evidence.\\n3. Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py --cov=backlog_core.operations --cov-report=term-missing -q -p no:cacheprovider` and record the `view_item`/`_live_lookup_id` coverage figure.\\n4. Run `git diff HEAD --stat` and confirm only the one test file is modified.\\n5. Run `git add plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` then `git commit -m \\\"test(backlog_core): cover view_item refresh control flow\\\"`.\",\"context_notes\":\"Architect spec section 8, \\\"New tests required\\\", enumerates the exact scenarios. Read it plus sections 4.4 and ADR-3 via `artifact_read(item_id=3275, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`.\\n\\nTarget test file: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py`. Follow that file's existing conventions \\u2014 `pytest-mock`'s `mocker: MockerFixture`, the Tests/How/Why docstring structure used by e.g. `test_list_items_refresh_calls_refresh_local_cache`, and its existing patch target style (`mocker.patch(\\\"backlog_core.operations.<name>\\\")`).\\n\\nT3's handoff contains the exact `_live_lookup_id()` implementation text \\u2014 read it before writing the id-resolution assertions, so your expected identifiers match what was actually implemented.\\n\\nCoverage target per spec section 8: 90% minimum on `view_item()`'s touched branches (business-logic tier in the repo's coverage convention).\\n## CORRECTION \\u2014 ADR-3 revised (read before starting)\\n\\nT3 discovered during implementation that the original ADR-3 premise was wrong: 52 existing tests in `backlog_core/tests/` (via the shared `_view_test_helpers.py::_configure_memory_view` fixture) already assert that a cached numeric-selector item is live-enriched UNCONDITIONALLY \\u2014 contradicting the original plan that `refresh` gates this case (Case A). The architect spec (`artifact_read(item_id=3275, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")`) has been corrected: `refresh` is now additive-only. Case A/B (cached item + numeric/#N/URL selector) stays unconditional, exactly as it behaved before this item \\u2014 do NOT write a test asserting `refresh=False` on a numeric selector skips the live call, that is FALSE under the corrected design. The only new conditional behavior is Case H (cached item + title-substring selector).\\n\\nYOUR REQUIREMENTS ARE REPLACED with this list (supersedes the original Requirements section above):\\n1. Cached item + title-substring selector + `refresh=True` -> `view_enrich_from_github` called, identifier argument equals the item's `number`/`issue`-derived id, NOT the raw title string.\\n2. Cached item + title-substring selector + `refresh=False` (new default) -> `view_enrich_from_github` NOT called. This is the true regression-risk case now \\u2014 it locks in that Case H is opt-in.\\n3. Cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` -> `view_enrich_from_github` IS called (regression guard confirming Case A stayed unconditional and was NOT accidentally gated \\u2014 this replaces the old scenario 2 which asserted the opposite).\\n4. No cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` -> live lookup still fires, no `ItemNotFoundError` (Case C/D, unchanged from original spec).\\n5. No cached item + beads nanoid + `refresh=False` -> live lookup still fires (Case E/F, unchanged from original spec).\\n6. Cached item + title selector + `refresh=True` + item has neither `number` nor `issue` set -> warning appended, no exception, `view_enrich_from_github` NOT called (unchanged from original spec).\\n\\nRead the corrected architect spec \\u00a74.4 and \\u00a78 in full before writing any test \\u2014 the truth table there is authoritative. Original scenario 2 (`refresh=False` on numeric selector -> NOT called) is WRONG and must not be implemented.\\n## Handoff\\n\\n## Five new test functions (TestViewItem)\\n\\n1. `test_view_item_title_selector_refresh_true_uses_item_identifier` \\u2014 Case H, refresh=True: `view_enrich_from_github` called with the item's issue-derived id (\\\"77\\\"), not the raw title.\\n2. `test_view_item_title_selector_refresh_false_skips_live_check` \\u2014 Case H, refresh=False (new default): `view_enrich_from_github` NOT called. **Primary regression-risk case.**\\n3. `test_view_item_numeric_selector_refresh_false_still_calls_enrich` \\u2014 Case A/B regression guard: numeric selector on a cached item still calls unconditionally (refresh is additive-only per corrected ADR-3).\\n4. `test_view_item_no_cached_item_numeric_selector_refresh_false_still_resolves` \\u2014 Case C/D regression guard (ADR-3): no local item + numeric selector still triggers a live lookup, no false `ItemNotFoundError`.\\n5. `test_view_item_refresh_true_no_identifier_appends_warning_without_call` \\u2014 item has no resolvable id (`issue=\\\"\\\"`), refresh=True: warning appended, `view_enrich_from_github` NOT called, no exception.\\n\\nScenario \\\"no cached item + beads nanoid + refresh=False\\\" (the plan's 6th listed scenario) already has pre-existing coverage via `TestViewItemBeadsNanoidUncached.test_view_item_beads_nanoid_uncached_calls_enrich` (calls `view_item(\\\"bd-e2f4\\\")` with the refresh=False default against a BeadsBackend and asserts the live call fires) \\u2014 per the task's revision rule, did not duplicate it; left a comment in the test file pointing to it instead. Net: 5 new test functions, matching the stale acceptance-criteria's \\\"exactly five\\\" count.\\n\\n## Mutation evidence (regression guards)\\n\\nAll three guard-relevant tests were mutation-checked by temporarily editing `operations.py`'s `view_item()`, confirming red, then reverting (verified `git diff HEAD -- .../operations.py` empty afterward):\\n\\n1. **Case H guard** (`test_view_item_title_selector_refresh_false_skips_live_check`): mutated `if issue_num or refresh:` to `if True:` (force unconditional). RED: `AssertionError: Expected 'view_enrich_from_github' to not have been called. Called 1 times.` Reverted -> green.\\n2. **Case C/D guard** (`test_view_item_no_cached_item_numeric_selector_refresh_false_still_resolves`): mutated `elif issue_num or get_config().backend.issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\":` to `elif refresh and (...)`. RED: `backlog_core.models.ItemNotFoundError: No item found for: 999`. Reverted -> green.\\n3. **Case A/B guard** (`test_view_item_numeric_selector_refresh_false_still_calls_enrich`): mutated the cached-item gate to effectively `if refresh:` (dropping the `issue_num` unconditional path). RED: `AssertionError: Expected 'view_enrich_from_github' to have been called once. Called 0 times.` Reverted -> green.\\n\\nFull file re-run after final revert: 150 passed (145 pre-existing + 5 new).\\n\\n## Coverage\\n\\n`view_item()` (lines 2876-2988): **100%** (30/30) after adding `show=\\\"1\\\"` / `show=\\\"not-a-number\\\"` to two of the new tests, which also exercises the pre-existing MCP str->int `show` conversion branches that had no coverage in this file.\\n\\n`_live_lookup_id()` (lines 2854-2873): **88.9%** (8/9) \\u2014 the one uncovered line is `return str(number)`, which T3's handoff documents as defensively unreachable: `BacklogItem` has no `.number` field (only `.issue: str`), so `getattr(item, \\\"number\\\", None)` always falls through to the `item.issue` branch today. This is a pre-existing model/code characteristic, not something a new test can reach without a production change (which is out of scope per this task's constraints). Combined average across both functions: 38/39 = 97.4%.\\n\\n## No scenario required a production change.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py -q -p no:cacheprovider --no-cov`: 150 passed, 0 failed.\\n- `uv run ruff check` and `uv run ruff format --diff` on the modified file: clean.\\n- `git diff HEAD --stat` after commit: only `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` (135 insertions), committed as `bc360962c`. (Note: this shared worktree had concurrent uncommitted T5 changes in `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` and `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` at commit time; those were temporarily set aside via a uniquely-tagged `git stash push -u` scoped to just those two paths, restored via `git stash apply` immediately after my commit, and the stash entry dropped only after confirming reapplication \\u2014 T5's in-progress work was never touched or lost.)\\n- No existing test was modified, skipped, or removed; collected count increased by exactly 5 (145 -> 150).\\n\",\"handoff\":\"Return:\\n- The five new test function names and the scenario each covers.\\n- The red/green mutation evidence for both regression guards (this is the core deliverable \\u2014 a guard without it is unverified).\\n- The measured coverage figure for `view_item()` and `_live_lookup_id()`.\\n- Any scenario that could not be tested without a production change, and what change would be needed.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"high\"},{\"id\":\"T5\",\"title\":\"Add MCP backlog_view and CLI list/view test coverage for the refresh parameter\",\"status\":\"in-progress\",\"agent\":\"python-engineering:python-pytest-architect\",\"dependencies\":[\"T2\",\"T3\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":2,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"fastmcp-creator:fastmcp-creator\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T21:46:53.557190+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-29T00:08:40.844716+00:00\",\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"## CoVe Checks\\n\\nKey claims to verify:\\n- Claim A: `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` has no pre-existing `list` or `view` coverage (the spec's Files-section audit finding).\\n- Claim B: each forwarding test fails when the forwarding kwarg is removed.\\n- Claim C: the CLI tests use the same `env=_CLI_ENV` and patch-target conventions as the file's existing tests, so they resolve the same backend.\\n\\nVerification questions:\\n1. Does `grep -n 'runner.invoke' plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` show any pre-existing `list` or `view` invocation? (Decomposition found only `add` and `sync` \\u2014 confirm this still holds after T1 and T3.)\\n2. When you remove `refresh=refresh` from `backlog_view`'s `to_thread` call, does your server test go red? Record the output.\\n3. When you remove `refresh=refresh` from the CLI `view` call, does your CLI test go red? Record the output.\\n4. What patch target do the existing tests in each file use for `operations`, and are you using the identical target string? A mismatched patch target silently produces a test that asserts nothing.\\n5. Does the CLI runner exit code get asserted (exit 0) in your new tests, so a Typer parameter-parsing error cannot masquerade as a pass?\\n\\nEvidence to collect: the grep output for question 1; both red/green mutation outputs; the patch-target strings used.\\n\\nRevision rule: if question 4 shows a patch-target mismatch, correct it and re-run the mutation check \\u2014 a test that stays green under mutation is not a test. If question 1 finds pre-existing coverage, extend it rather than duplicating, and note it.\",\"description\":\"The `refresh` parameter now exists on three surfaces above `operations`: MCP `backlog_view`, CLI `view`, and (post-rename) CLI `list`. None is covered. `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py` currently tests only `backlog add` and `backlog sync` \\u2014 `list` and `view` have zero coverage, so the rename in T1 and the new flag in T3 are both unguarded at the CLI boundary.\\n\\nThis task adds forwarding tests at both boundaries. It is a boundary-contract task: it proves the parameter reaches `op